it's called the mckinney fire it started  on friday grew from 1 to 160 square  kilometers in 24 hours and is now  covering well over 200 square kilometers  and continuing to spread  a mandatory evacuation order was issued  an estimated two thousand people left  their home saturday and another five  hundred have been evacuated in the  course of sunday  many leaving behind their possessions  like this 81 year old my house is gone  all my furniture all my clothes shoes  coats boots  everything's gone  some decided to leave before the  mandatory evacuation and managed to save  some of their belongings  yeah we got out before the fires  actually they gave us a red flag to get  out because we don't want to be there to  when they do say get out have 15 minutes  to get out and then we got all our shows  packed up ready to go so we get out of  there as soon as possible the swirling  winds made the course of the fire  impossible to predict yeah i mean it  could come from any angle at this point  it's just a matter of where the winds  take it  over 60 hikers who are on the popular  pacific crest trail were safely rescued  they had about 20 feet of visibility on  the trail at the time that they you know  chose to call in and try to get some  help  the mckinney fire is by far the largest  but across the west of the united states  more fires are flaring up  erratic weather is threatening to bring  dry thunderstorms with dangerous  lightning but little to no actual rain  and above all the soaring heat is  creating the ideal conditions for fires  to start and spread  mike hannah al jazeera
 

